@startuml OpenCodeTopology
' purpose: the OpenCode native crew layout and approved automatic session policy
' covers: defs/opencode/**
' covers: defs/subagents/_frontmatter/opencode/**
' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh
' Native migration and pending acceptance: _spec/defs/opencode/native-v2-integration.puml
' Crew/auth decisions: _spec/defs/opencode/opencode-paradigm.puml
' Automatic approval is an approved target, not evidence that its exact setting passed tests.
' Legacy local-model e2e caught cloud fallback without an ollama provider definition.
' The shared LSP detector emits lang|count|cmd|arg...|extcsv; native rendering keeps
' every command field between the count and trailing extension CSV.
' Register: manual normalized word/syllable counts; two sentences per reasoning note.
' FK: note right of Crew; words=31 syllables=57; FK 12.2
' FK: note right of Env; words=30 syllables=56; FK 12.3
' FK: note right of Lsp; words=30 syllables=53; FK 11.1
!includeurl https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/refs/heads/main/proveo.iuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

left to right direction

title OpenCode Topology — GStack Subagent Crew

actor "Human\nrisk instructions + review" as Human
actor "Primary Agent\n(Team Lead)" as Lead

package "Harness Layer" as Harness {
 component "entrypoint.sh" as Entrypoint <<script>>
 component ".env + requested local-provider wiring" as Env <<logic>>
 component "LSP auto-detect" as Lsp <<logic>>
 component "shared native bootstrap + subagents" as Seed <<logic>>
 component "AGENTS.md\n(team rules)" as AgentsMd <<prompt>>
}

package "Primary Agents" as Primaries {
 component "plan\n(edit + shell deny)" as Plan <<agent>>
 component "build\n(edit allow; native shell ask rule)" as Build <<agent>>
 component "opencode session\napproved automatic approval mode" as Policy <<logic>>
}

package "Subagent Crew" as Crew {
 component "@architect\n(design before code)" as Architect <<subagent>>
 component "@backend / @frontend\n(domain advisors; no edit/shell)" as Domain <<subagent>>
 component "@devops / @sre\n(advisors; no edit/shell)" as Ops <<subagent>>
 component "@adversarial-reviewer\n(find bugs, no fixes)" as Reviewer <<subagent>>
 component "@security-reviewer" as Security <<subagent>>
 component "@spec-keeper\n(_spec/ changes)" as SpecKeeper <<subagent>>
 component "@systems-design\n@monorepo-coordinator" as Systems <<subagent>>
}

package "Verification Layer" as Verify {
 component "detect test/lint/build cmds" as Detect <<logic>>
 component "compaction.auto" as Context <<logic>>
 component "review gates\nBLOCKER/HIGH stop completion" as Gates <<logic>>
}

Human --> Entrypoint : launch
Entrypoint --> Env
Entrypoint --> Lsp
Entrypoint --> Seed
Entrypoint --> AgentsMd
Lead --> Plan : delegate planning
Lead --> Build : delegate implementation
Seed --> Policy : approved session policy; validation pending
Policy --> Build : automatic asks, not per-shell HITL
Build --> Architect : request design
Build --> Domain : request domain advice
Domain --> Reviewer : request review
Reviewer --> Security : security review if needed
Lead --> Verify : run detected commands
Verify --> Gates : enforce before done
Human --> Lead : risk instructions + merge review

note right of Crew
  Shared Markdown bodies define the advisor crew
  without granting implementation rights.
  The lead routes reviews by concern, while the
  spec-keeper prompt confines its existing edit
  exception to the approved documentation scope.
end note

note bottom of Primaries
  plan = edit + shell denied
  build = edit allowed; shell rule ask
end note

note bottom of Policy
  Approved session policy is automatic.
  Exact native setting awaits validation.
end note

note right of Env
  The default seed names no model so the harness
  retains model selection. An explicit
  local-model request registers its provider
  and selects that model instead of reviving
  the retired role-to-model bridge.
end note

note right of Lsp
  The shared detector emits command fields
  followed by the extension list for each
  language. The native writer preserves those
  boundaries when building LSP entries, so
  arguments cannot become file extensions.
end note


@enduml
